// ── fjord-app · connect_seerr.slint ──────────────────────────────────────────
//   ConnectSeerrScreen  free-floating overlay, mounted + fade-gated by
//                       main.slint (gate30 := FadeGate { show: AppState.show-
//                       connect-seerr; }, opacity passed in from there — same
//                       pattern as PlaylistPicker/ContextMenu; the FadeGate
//                       instance must live at the mount site, not inside this
//                       component, or delayed-unmount never gets a chance to
//                       run before the whole component is destroyed). Server
//                       URL LineEdit shared across all 4 methods; a 4-tab
//                       method selector switches which fields show below it.
//                       All 4 methods converge on AppState's on-success path
//                       (seerr_auth.rs) which closes this screen. Errors stay
//                       on-screen (mirrors LoginScreen), not a toast.
//
//   Full D-pad keyboard navigation + on-screen alphanumeric keyboard,
//   2026-08-23 — this screen had ZERO keyboard nav before (pure mouse +
//   native Tab order); see app_state.slint's connect-seerr-zone doc comment
//   for the full zone design (mirrors login-zone's shape — dispatch lives
//   inline in keys.rs's show_connect_seerr tier, not a delegate function the
//   way ProfileEditScreen's larger zone system does). MethodTab gets a real
//   kbd-focused prop (bound to connect-seerr-zone == 0 on all 4 instances —
//   the D-pad cursor for the tab row and the currently-selected tab ARE the
//   same value, connect-seerr-method, so there's no separate per-tab cursor
//   concept) plus the same border-ring + PressPulse treatment every other
//   keyboard-navigable element in this app already has, mirroring NavItem's
//   own shape (active && kbd-focused gates the flash). Every submit/"Get
//   Code" button gets kbd-focused too, bound to whichever zone value
//   resolves to "the last zone in the list" for its own tab (2 for Quick
//   Connect, 3 for API key, 4 for Jellyfin/Local) — see
//   seerr_auth::existing_connect_seerr_zones' own doc comment for why that's
//   always the button, never a text field, regardless of tab.
//
//   Real scoping constraint found while building this, not anticipated by
//   the plan: the 5 method-specific fields (key-input/jf-user/jf-pass/
//   local-email/local-pass) each sit inside their own `if connect-seerr-
//   method == N:` conditional — Slint's hard rule that "an element declared
//   inside an if block is not a valid identifier outside it" (confirmed at
//   COMPILE TIME while writing this, not a style choice) means none of them
//   can be referenced from a shared, root-level function/tracker the way
//   login.slint's 3 always-mounted fields can. Fixed with a relay: root-
//   level dispatch-onscreen-key handles "done" and the always-mounted
//   url-input directly, but relays anything else (one of the 5 method-
//   specific targets) through a payload+counter pair (_relay-key/-seq, same
//   shape as onscreen-keyboard-physical-key/-seq — needed so `changed`
//   fires even on a repeated identical key) that each text-field-bearing
//   conditional block picks up with its OWN local mirror tracker, scoped
//   to see only its own field(s). The same split applies to focus-restore-
//   on-close and zone→focus hand-off (each conditional block gets its own
//   small local trackers for these too) and to Enter-driven submit (each
//   text-field tab's own local _pulse-mirror-equivalent calls its own
//   connect-seerr-* callback; Quick Connect's Get Code needs no such local
//   copy since it only ever references the always-mounted url-input, so it
//   stays at root scope). Referencing an UNCONDITIONALLY-mounted sibling
//   (url-input) FROM INSIDE a conditional block is fine — confirmed by the
//   compiler accepting it in every one of the 3 text-field tabs' own submit
//   buttons — it's only the reverse direction (conditional → outside) that's
//   the hard rule.
//
//   root.close-screen() is the one choke point every close path (backdrop
//   click, the ✕ button, and every field's own Escape branch) routes
//   through — unconditionally clears the on-screen keyboard's 3 properties
//   alongside show-connect-seerr, mirroring close_login_screen/
//   close_profile_edit_screen's established precedent (Bonfire Phase 3's
//   original code review, Finding 1): without this, closing the screen
//   while the on-screen keyboard is open would leave AppState.show-
//   onscreen-keyboard stuck true — that gate runs before EVERY other
//   screen's own tier in keys.rs, so a stuck keyboard permanently swallows
//   all subsequent input app-wide, not just on this screen. keys.rs's own
//   Rust-side close sites (Escape at zone -1/0, zone -1's own Enter) do the
//   Rust-side equivalent directly (this Slint function can't be called from
//   Rust) — kept in sync by hand, same as every other Rust/Slint dual-side
//   mechanism in this app.
//
//   The 3 `accepted =>` handlers key-input/jf-pass/local-pass used to have
//   are gone (2026-08-23) — physical Enter now opens the on-screen keyboard
//   on every field, matching Login's own identical removal and the same
//   reasoning ("if they press enter on a textfield they want to enter it to
//   type"); submitting moves entirely to each tab's own button, reachable
//   via Down from the last field once the keyboard is closed.
//
//   Coexistence guard (is-my-onscreen-target()) — this screen isn't
//   permanently mounted the way Browse/Discover are, but it IS a
//   free-floating overlay reachable independent of whatever's underneath,
//   so its QwertyKeyboard mount condition and _physical-key-mirror both
//   check the target explicitly rather than bare show-onscreen-keyboard
//   alone, same discipline established for ProfileEditScreen/Discover/
//   Browse/PlaylistPicker (see CLAUDE.md's own "coexistence guard" write-up
//   for the full reasoning — without it, two screens' keyboard interactions
//   could cross-fire on each other's keystrokes).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
import { Theme } from "theme.slint";
import { AppState } from "app_state.slint";
import { FjordButton, FieldFocusWrap, QwertyKeyboard, PressPulse } from "widgets.slint";
import { LineEdit } from "std-widgets.slint";

component MethodTab inherits Rectangle {
    in property <string> label;
    in property <bool>   active;
    in property <bool>   kbd-focused;
    callback clicked;

    height: 34px;
    border-radius: Theme.radius;
    background: active ? Theme.accent : (ta.has-hover ? Theme.surface : transparent);
    border-width: (ta.pressed || pulse.pulsing) ? 3px : 0px;
    border-color: Theme.focus-border;
    animate border-width, background { duration: 90ms * AppState.settings-animation-speed; easing: ease-out-expo; }
    pulse := PressPulse { trigger: AppState.kb-activate-pulse; active: root.active && root.kbd-focused; }

    ta := TouchArea { clicked => { root.clicked(); } }
    Text {
        text: label;
        color: active ? Theme.bg : Theme.text;
        font-size: 12px;
        font-weight: 600;
        horizontal-alignment: center;
        vertical-alignment: center;
    }
}

export component ConnectSeerrScreen inherits Rectangle {
    background: #000000aa;

    function close-screen() {
        AppState.show-connect-seerr = false;
        AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard = false;
        AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target = "";
        AppState.onscreen-keyboard-cursor = 0;
    }

    // Payload+counter relay for keystrokes bound for one of the 5
    // conditionally-mounted method-specific fields — see this file's own
    // header doc comment for why root-level code can't reach them directly.
    property <string> _relay-key: "";
    property <int> _relay-key-seq: 0;

    pure function is-my-onscreen-target() -> bool {
        AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-url"
            || AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-key"
            || AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-jf-user"
            || AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-jf-pass"
            || AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-local-email"
            || AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-local-pass"
    }

    function dispatch-onscreen-key(k: string) {
        if k == "done" {
            AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard = false;
        } else if AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-url" {
            url-input.text = k == "backspace"
                ? AppState.onscreen-keyboard-trim-last(url-input.text)
                : url-input.text + k;
            let len = AppState.onscreen-keyboard-byte-len(url-input.text);
            url-input.set-selection-offsets(len, len);
        } else {
            root._relay-key = k;
            root._relay-key-seq += 1;
        }
    }

    close-ta := TouchArea {
        clicked => { root.close-screen(); AppState.refocus(); }
    }

    card := Rectangle {
        width:         min(460px, parent.width - 48px);
        height:        inner.preferred-height;
        x:             (parent.width  - self.width)  / 2;
        y:             (parent.height - self.height) / 2;
        background:    Theme.surface;
        border-radius: Theme.radius-lg;
        drop-shadow-blur:  28px;
        drop-shadow-color: #00000070;

        // Swallow clicks so the backdrop TouchArea above doesn't close the
        // card when interacting with it.
        card-ta := TouchArea {}

        inner := VerticalLayout {
            padding: Theme.sp-xl;
            spacing: Theme.sp;

            HorizontalLayout {
                alignment: space-between;
                Text {
                    text: "Connect Seerr";
                    color: Theme.text;
                    font-size: 20px;
                    font-weight: 700;
                }
                FjordButton {
                    text: "✕";
                    width: 32px;
                    height: 32px;
                    kbd-focused: AppState.connect-seerr-zone == -1;
                    clicked => {
                        AppState.connect-seerr-zone = -1;
                        root.close-screen();
                        AppState.refocus();
                    }
                }
            }

            url-field-wrap := FieldFocusWrap {
                focused: AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard && AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 1;
                url-input := LineEdit {
                    x: 2px; y: 2px;
                    width: parent.width - 4px;
                    height: parent.height - 4px;
                    placeholder-text: "Seerr URL  (e.g. seerr.example.com or 192.168.1.10:5055)";
                    changed has-focus => {
                        if self.has-focus {
                            AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 1;
                            if AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard {
                                AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target = "connect-seerr-url";
                                AppState.onscreen-keyboard-cursor = 0;
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    key-pressed(event) => {
                        if event.text == "\u{1b}" {
                            root.close-screen();
                            AppState.refocus();
                            return accept;
                        }
                        if event.text == "\u{F700}" {
                            AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 0;
                            AppState.refocus();
                            return accept;
                        }
                        // Down leaves this field entirely and hands off via
                        // connect-seerr-zone + refocus() rather than a
                        // direct .focus() call on whichever field/button is
                        // next — that target may be one of the 5
                        // conditionally-mounted method-specific fields this
                        // shared field can't reference directly (see this
                        // file's own header doc comment); each target's own
                        // local zone-mirror tracker (or, for a button zone,
                        // keys.rs's own Rust-side dispatch) picks up the
                        // zone change from there. While Quick Connect is
                        // polling there's nothing below the URL field at
                        // all, so Down is a no-op in that one state.
                        if event.text == "\u{F701}" {
                            if !(AppState.connect-seerr-method == 2 && AppState.connect-seerr-qc-polling) {
                                AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 2;
                                AppState.refocus();
                            }
                            return accept;
                        }
                        if event.text == "\u{000a}" {
                            AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target = "connect-seerr-url";
                            AppState.onscreen-keyboard-cursor = 0;
                            AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard = true;
                            AppState.refocus();
                            return accept;
                        }
                        return reject;
                    }
                }
            }

            HorizontalLayout {
                spacing: 6px;
                MethodTab {
                    label: "API Key"; active: AppState.connect-seerr-method == 0;
                    kbd-focused: AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 0;
                    clicked => { AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 0; AppState.connect-seerr-method = 0; AppState.connect-seerr-error = ""; }
                }
                MethodTab {
                    label: "Jellyfin"; active: AppState.connect-seerr-method == 1;
                    kbd-focused: AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 0;
                    clicked => { AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 0; AppState.connect-seerr-method = 1; AppState.connect-seerr-error = ""; }
                }
                MethodTab {
                    label: "Quick Connect"; active: AppState.connect-seerr-method == 2;
                    kbd-focused: AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 0;
                    clicked => { AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 0; AppState.connect-seerr-method = 2; AppState.connect-seerr-error = ""; }
                }
                MethodTab {
                    label: "Local Account"; active: AppState.connect-seerr-method == 3;
                    kbd-focused: AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 0;
                    clicked => { AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 0; AppState.connect-seerr-method = 3; AppState.connect-seerr-error = ""; }
                }
            }

            Rectangle { height: 2px; }

            // ── Method 0: static API key ─────────────────────────────────
            if AppState.connect-seerr-method == 0: VerticalLayout {
                spacing: Theme.sp;
                Text {
                    text: "Paste an API key generated in Seerr's own admin Settings.";
                    color: Theme.text-muted;
                    font-size: 12px;
                    wrap: word-wrap;
                }
                key-field-wrap := FieldFocusWrap {
                    focused: AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard && AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 2;
                    key-input := LineEdit {
                        x: 2px; y: 2px;
                        width: parent.width - 4px;
                        height: parent.height - 4px;
                        placeholder-text: "API key";
                        input-type: password;
                        // No `accepted =>` handler (removed 2026-08-23) —
                        // see this file's own header doc comment.
                        changed has-focus => {
                            if self.has-focus {
                                AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 2;
                                if AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard {
                                    AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target = "connect-seerr-key";
                                    AppState.onscreen-keyboard-cursor = 0;
                                }
                            }
                        }
                        key-pressed(event) => {
                            if event.text == "\u{1b}" {
                                root.close-screen();
                                AppState.refocus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            if event.text == "\u{F700}" {
                                url-input.focus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            if event.text == "\u{F701}" {
                                AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 3;
                                AppState.refocus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            if event.text == "\u{000a}" {
                                AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target = "connect-seerr-key";
                                AppState.onscreen-keyboard-cursor = 0;
                                AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard = true;
                                AppState.refocus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            return reject;
                        }
                    }
                }
                FjordButton {
                    text: AppState.connect-seerr-busy ? "Connecting…" : "Save";
                    enabled: !AppState.connect-seerr-busy;
                    kbd-focused: AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 3;
                    clicked => {
                        AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 3;
                        AppState.connect-seerr-api-key(url-input.text, key-input.text);
                    }
                }

                // Local mirrors — this block's own fields (key-input) are
                // conditionally mounted and can't be reached from root-level
                // code, so this tab carries its own small copy of the same
                // relay/close/zone/pulse idiom root-level fields get for
                // free (see this file's own header doc comment).
                property <int> _relay-mirror: root._relay-key-seq;
                changed _relay-mirror => {
                    if AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-key" {
                        key-input.text = root._relay-key == "backspace"
                            ? AppState.onscreen-keyboard-trim-last(key-input.text)
                            : key-input.text + root._relay-key;
                        let len = AppState.onscreen-keyboard-byte-len(key-input.text);
                        key-input.set-selection-offsets(len, len);
                    }
                }
                property <bool> _kb-close-local-mirror: AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard;
                changed _kb-close-local-mirror => {
                    if !_kb-close-local-mirror && AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-key" {
                        key-input.focus();
                    }
                }
                property <int> _zone-local-mirror: AppState.connect-seerr-zone;
                changed _zone-local-mirror => {
                    if _zone-local-mirror == 2 { key-input.focus(); }
                }
                property <int> _pulse-local-mirror: AppState.kb-activate-pulse;
                changed _pulse-local-mirror => {
                    if AppState.show-connect-seerr && AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 3 {
                        AppState.connect-seerr-api-key(url-input.text, key-input.text);
                    }
                }
            }

            // ── Method 1: Jellyfin username/password ─────────────────────
            if AppState.connect-seerr-method == 1: VerticalLayout {
                spacing: Theme.sp;
                jf-user-wrap := FieldFocusWrap {
                    focused: AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard && AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 2;
                    jf-user := LineEdit {
                        x: 2px; y: 2px;
                        width: parent.width - 4px;
                        height: parent.height - 4px;
                        placeholder-text: "Jellyfin username";
                        changed has-focus => {
                            if self.has-focus {
                                AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 2;
                                if AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard {
                                    AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target = "connect-seerr-jf-user";
                                    AppState.onscreen-keyboard-cursor = 0;
                                }
                            }
                        }
                        key-pressed(event) => {
                            if event.text == "\u{1b}" {
                                root.close-screen();
                                AppState.refocus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            if event.text == "\u{F700}" {
                                url-input.focus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            if event.text == "\u{F701}" {
                                jf-pass.focus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            if event.text == "\u{000a}" {
                                AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target = "connect-seerr-jf-user";
                                AppState.onscreen-keyboard-cursor = 0;
                                AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard = true;
                                AppState.refocus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            return reject;
                        }
                    }
                }
                jf-pass-wrap := FieldFocusWrap {
                    focused: AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard && AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 3;
                    jf-pass := LineEdit {
                        x: 2px; y: 2px;
                        width: parent.width - 4px;
                        height: parent.height - 4px;
                        placeholder-text: "Jellyfin password";
                        input-type: password;
                        // No `accepted =>` handler (removed 2026-08-23) —
                        // see this file's own header doc comment.
                        changed has-focus => {
                            if self.has-focus {
                                AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 3;
                                if AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard {
                                    AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target = "connect-seerr-jf-pass";
                                    AppState.onscreen-keyboard-cursor = 0;
                                }
                            }
                        }
                        key-pressed(event) => {
                            if event.text == "\u{1b}" {
                                root.close-screen();
                                AppState.refocus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            if event.text == "\u{F700}" {
                                jf-user.focus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            if event.text == "\u{F701}" {
                                AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 4;
                                AppState.refocus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            if event.text == "\u{000a}" {
                                AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target = "connect-seerr-jf-pass";
                                AppState.onscreen-keyboard-cursor = 0;
                                AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard = true;
                                AppState.refocus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            return reject;
                        }
                    }
                }
                FjordButton {
                    text: AppState.connect-seerr-busy ? "Signing in…" : "Sign In";
                    enabled: !AppState.connect-seerr-busy;
                    kbd-focused: AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 4;
                    clicked => {
                        AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 4;
                        AppState.connect-seerr-jellyfin(url-input.text, jf-user.text, jf-pass.text);
                    }
                }

                // Local mirrors — see the API key tab's own identical block
                // for the full "why" (this file's header doc comment).
                property <int> _relay-mirror: root._relay-key-seq;
                changed _relay-mirror => {
                    if AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-jf-user" {
                        jf-user.text = root._relay-key == "backspace"
                            ? AppState.onscreen-keyboard-trim-last(jf-user.text)
                            : jf-user.text + root._relay-key;
                        let len = AppState.onscreen-keyboard-byte-len(jf-user.text);
                        jf-user.set-selection-offsets(len, len);
                    } else if AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-jf-pass" {
                        jf-pass.text = root._relay-key == "backspace"
                            ? AppState.onscreen-keyboard-trim-last(jf-pass.text)
                            : jf-pass.text + root._relay-key;
                        let len = AppState.onscreen-keyboard-byte-len(jf-pass.text);
                        jf-pass.set-selection-offsets(len, len);
                    }
                }
                property <bool> _kb-close-local-mirror: AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard;
                changed _kb-close-local-mirror => {
                    if !_kb-close-local-mirror {
                        if AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-jf-user" { jf-user.focus(); }
                        else if AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-jf-pass" { jf-pass.focus(); }
                    }
                }
                property <int> _zone-local-mirror: AppState.connect-seerr-zone;
                changed _zone-local-mirror => {
                    if _zone-local-mirror == 2 { jf-user.focus(); }
                    else if _zone-local-mirror == 3 { jf-pass.focus(); }
                }
                property <int> _pulse-local-mirror: AppState.kb-activate-pulse;
                changed _pulse-local-mirror => {
                    if AppState.show-connect-seerr && AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 4 {
                        AppState.connect-seerr-jellyfin(url-input.text, jf-user.text, jf-pass.text);
                    }
                }
            }

            // ── Method 2: Jellyfin Quick Connect ──────────────────────────
            if AppState.connect-seerr-method == 2: VerticalLayout {
                spacing: Theme.sp;
                if !AppState.connect-seerr-qc-polling: VerticalLayout {
                    spacing: Theme.sp;
                    Text {
                        text: "Passwordless — approve a code from inside your Jellyfin app or web UI.";
                        color: Theme.text-muted;
                        font-size: 12px;
                        wrap: word-wrap;
                    }
                    FjordButton {
                        text: AppState.connect-seerr-busy ? "Requesting code…" : "Get Code";
                        enabled: !AppState.connect-seerr-busy;
                        kbd-focused: AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 2;
                        clicked => {
                            AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 2;
                            AppState.connect-seerr-quickconnect-start(url-input.text);
                        }
                    }
                }
                if AppState.connect-seerr-qc-polling: VerticalLayout {
                    spacing: Theme.sp;
                    alignment: center;
                    Text {
                        text: AppState.connect-seerr-qc-code;
                        color: Theme.accent;
                        font-size: 40px;
                        font-weight: 700;
                        letter-spacing: 6px;
                        horizontal-alignment: center;
                    }
                    Text {
                        text: "Enter this code in Jellyfin's Quick Connect settings — waiting for approval…";
                        color: Theme.text-muted;
                        font-size: 12px;
                        horizontal-alignment: center;
                        wrap: word-wrap;
                    }
                    qc-poll-timer := Timer {
                        interval: 2000ms;
                        running: AppState.connect-seerr-qc-polling;
                        triggered => {
                            AppState.connect-seerr-quickconnect-poll(url-input.text, AppState.connect-seerr-qc-secret);
                        }
                    }
                }
                // No local mirrors needed here — Get Code only ever
                // references url-input, which is unconditionally mounted
                // and already reachable from root scope; the root-level
                // _pulse-mirror below dispatches it directly.
            }

            // ── Method 3: local Seerr account ─────────────────────────────
            if AppState.connect-seerr-method == 3: VerticalLayout {
                spacing: Theme.sp;
                local-email-wrap := FieldFocusWrap {
                    focused: AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard && AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 2;
                    local-email := LineEdit {
                        x: 2px; y: 2px;
                        width: parent.width - 4px;
                        height: parent.height - 4px;
                        placeholder-text: "Email";
                        changed has-focus => {
                            if self.has-focus {
                                AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 2;
                                if AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard {
                                    AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target = "connect-seerr-local-email";
                                    AppState.onscreen-keyboard-cursor = 0;
                                }
                            }
                        }
                        key-pressed(event) => {
                            if event.text == "\u{1b}" {
                                root.close-screen();
                                AppState.refocus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            if event.text == "\u{F700}" {
                                url-input.focus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            if event.text == "\u{F701}" {
                                local-pass.focus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            if event.text == "\u{000a}" {
                                AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target = "connect-seerr-local-email";
                                AppState.onscreen-keyboard-cursor = 0;
                                AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard = true;
                                AppState.refocus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            return reject;
                        }
                    }
                }
                local-pass-wrap := FieldFocusWrap {
                    focused: AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard && AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 3;
                    local-pass := LineEdit {
                        x: 2px; y: 2px;
                        width: parent.width - 4px;
                        height: parent.height - 4px;
                        placeholder-text: "Password";
                        input-type: password;
                        // No `accepted =>` handler (removed 2026-08-23) —
                        // see this file's own header doc comment.
                        changed has-focus => {
                            if self.has-focus {
                                AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 3;
                                if AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard {
                                    AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target = "connect-seerr-local-pass";
                                    AppState.onscreen-keyboard-cursor = 0;
                                }
                            }
                        }
                        key-pressed(event) => {
                            if event.text == "\u{1b}" {
                                root.close-screen();
                                AppState.refocus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            if event.text == "\u{F700}" {
                                local-email.focus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            if event.text == "\u{F701}" {
                                AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 4;
                                AppState.refocus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            if event.text == "\u{000a}" {
                                AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target = "connect-seerr-local-pass";
                                AppState.onscreen-keyboard-cursor = 0;
                                AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard = true;
                                AppState.refocus();
                                return accept;
                            }
                            return reject;
                        }
                    }
                }
                FjordButton {
                    text: AppState.connect-seerr-busy ? "Signing in…" : "Sign In";
                    enabled: !AppState.connect-seerr-busy;
                    kbd-focused: AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 4;
                    clicked => {
                        AppState.connect-seerr-zone = 4;
                        AppState.connect-seerr-local(url-input.text, local-email.text, local-pass.text);
                    }
                }

                // Local mirrors — see the API key tab's own identical block
                // for the full "why" (this file's header doc comment).
                property <int> _relay-mirror: root._relay-key-seq;
                changed _relay-mirror => {
                    if AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-local-email" {
                        local-email.text = root._relay-key == "backspace"
                            ? AppState.onscreen-keyboard-trim-last(local-email.text)
                            : local-email.text + root._relay-key;
                        let len = AppState.onscreen-keyboard-byte-len(local-email.text);
                        local-email.set-selection-offsets(len, len);
                    } else if AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-local-pass" {
                        local-pass.text = root._relay-key == "backspace"
                            ? AppState.onscreen-keyboard-trim-last(local-pass.text)
                            : local-pass.text + root._relay-key;
                        let len = AppState.onscreen-keyboard-byte-len(local-pass.text);
                        local-pass.set-selection-offsets(len, len);
                    }
                }
                property <bool> _kb-close-local-mirror: AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard;
                changed _kb-close-local-mirror => {
                    if !_kb-close-local-mirror {
                        if AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-local-email" { local-email.focus(); }
                        else if AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-local-pass" { local-pass.focus(); }
                    }
                }
                property <int> _zone-local-mirror: AppState.connect-seerr-zone;
                changed _zone-local-mirror => {
                    if _zone-local-mirror == 2 { local-email.focus(); }
                    else if _zone-local-mirror == 3 { local-pass.focus(); }
                }
                property <int> _pulse-local-mirror: AppState.kb-activate-pulse;
                changed _pulse-local-mirror => {
                    if AppState.show-connect-seerr && AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 4 {
                        AppState.connect-seerr-local(url-input.text, local-email.text, local-pass.text);
                    }
                }
            }

            if AppState.connect-seerr-error != "": Text {
                text: AppState.connect-seerr-error;
                color: Theme.error;
                font-size: 12px;
                horizontal-alignment: center;
                wrap: word-wrap;
            }
        }
    }

    // On-screen alphanumeric keyboard (2026-08-23, full rollout beyond
    // Login) — positioned below the card, mirroring login.slint's own
    // placement/shape exactly, including the coexistence guard (see this
    // file's own header doc comment).
    if AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard && root.is-my-onscreen-target(): QwertyKeyboard {
        x: (parent.width - self.width) / 2;
        y: card.y + card.height + 16px;
        cursor: AppState.onscreen-keyboard-cursor;
        active: AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard;
        key-pressed(k) => { root.dispatch-onscreen-key(k); }
    }

    // Restores real native focus to url-input the instant the keyboard
    // closes — same idiom as login.slint's own _kb-close-mirror. The 5
    // method-specific fields each have their OWN local copy of this same
    // idiom inside their own conditional block (see this file's header doc
    // comment) since they can't be referenced from here.
    property <bool> _kb-close-mirror: AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard;
    changed _kb-close-mirror => {
        if !_kb-close-mirror && AppState.onscreen-keyboard-target == "connect-seerr-url" {
            url-input.focus();
        }
    }

    // Physical-keyboard passthrough — same idiom as login.slint's own
    // _physical-key-mirror. dispatch-onscreen-key itself handles routing
    // to url-input directly or relaying to whichever conditional block owns
    // the current target, so this needs no target-specific logic of its
    // own beyond the existing coexistence guard.
    property <int> _physical-key-mirror: AppState.onscreen-keyboard-physical-key-seq;
    changed _physical-key-mirror => {
        if AppState.show-onscreen-keyboard && root.is-my-onscreen-target() {
            root.dispatch-onscreen-key(AppState.onscreen-keyboard-physical-key);
        }
    }

    // Zone → url-input focus hand-off for whenever keys.rs's own
    // show_connect_seerr tier sets connect-seerr-zone back to 1 (it can
    // only SET the zone value, never call a named element's .focus()
    // method directly — same limitation login-zone's own _zone-mirror
    // already works around). The method-specific zones (2/3/4) are each
    // handled by their own conditional block's local zone mirror instead.
    property <int> _zone-mirror: AppState.connect-seerr-zone;
    changed _zone-mirror => {
        if _zone-mirror == 1 { url-input.focus(); }
    }

    // Zone-2's own D-pad Enter on Quick Connect's "Get Code" button has no
    // Rust-side arm — the actual quickconnect-start call needs a live
    // url-input.text value Rust can't read, same "Rust can only bump
    // kb-activate-pulse, a Slint-side changed tracker does the real work"
    // pattern login-zone's own zone 4 (Connect) already uses. The other 3
    // tabs' own submit buttons have their own LOCAL copy of this same
    // tracker (see this file's header doc comment) since their own
    // zone/method combination can't be checked from root scope without
    // also needing to reference their conditionally-mounted fields. Zone -1
    // (close) is handled directly in keys.rs instead — closing needs no
    // live text at all, so there's no reason to route it through this
    // indirection.
    property <int> _pulse-mirror: AppState.kb-activate-pulse;
    changed _pulse-mirror => {
        if AppState.show-connect-seerr && AppState.connect-seerr-method == 2
                && AppState.connect-seerr-zone == 2 && !AppState.connect-seerr-qc-polling {
            AppState.connect-seerr-quickconnect-start(url-input.text);
        }
    }
}
